## Authority this case is graded against

* **X960 platform support TPS** (`https://wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php/X960_platform_support_TPS`),
  fetched 2026-10-20 13:3x NZDT.  The case-title number maps to a TPS row with the constant
  -2 offset group C verified:

      TPS row 276 | Management | TACACS+ | Authentication | Priority 1 | Supported: Yes

  => TACACS+ authentication is **declared supported** on this platform, so an absent
  behaviour here would be a FINDING, not a platform limit.

* **"TACACS+ AAA" TFS**, project 1599
  (`https://wiki.atlnz.lc/awpwiki/index.php/TACACS%2B_AAA_TFS`), fetched 2026-10-20.
  The specifications this case is graded against:
  - **S1599.1.010** -- authentication messages sent to the TACACS+ server conform to the
    TACACS+ Authentication REQUEST packet format.
  - **S1599.1.004** -- with multiple servers configured, attempts are made **sequentially in
    the order the servers appear in the running config**, until a positive reply arrives
    within the timeout or the pool is exhausted; failure to communicate with all of them is
    logged.
  - **S1599.1.001/.002/.003** -- failure to communicate with the server produces an error
    message on the console and the failed attempt is logged.
  - **S1599.1.011 - .016** (enable authentication) -- **NOT MEASURED**, deliberately; the
    reason is set out under "NOT MEASURED, and why" at the end of this log.
  Feature background: the TACACS+ Feature Page records that AW+ TACACS+ is PAM-based
  (`pam_tacplus`) and that the protocol runs over **TCP port 49** with the body encrypted.

## Objective (designed by the tester)

Prove that this DUT can authenticate a CLI login against an external TACACS+ server: that a
user that exists ONLY on the server is admitted, that the DUT really spoke TACACS+ on the
wire to do it, that the server's answer -- not the local database -- decided the outcome, and
that each failure mode (wrong password, unknown user, wrong shared key, unreachable server)
has its own distinguishable signature.  Then prove the feature can be removed and leaves
nothing behind.

