    awplus# configure terminal
    awplus(config)# tacacs-server host 10.38.22.33 key testing123
    awplus(config)# aaa authentication login default group tacacs+ local
    awplus(config)# end

`cfg.py` exit 0; no `% ` line from either command.  Read back:

    awplus# show running-config | (relevant lines)
    username manager privilege 15 password 8 $5$bJozIP4D$orvkW78S6QHN65L3EGGJpHS...
    username tacuser privilege 15 password 8 $5$Qpzm8mltSdgsRkSS$lZGZxNuNlbEC3Fa...
    tacacs-server host 10.38.22.33 key 9 kh3afeSqzrMfJtQogCRezF0CmP35QlDTDuTr0FNzz7I=
    aaa authentication enable default local
    aaa authentication login default group tacacs+ local

    awplus# show tacacs+
    TACACS+ Global Configuration
      Source Interface    : not configured
      Timeout             : 5 sec

    Server Host/                                  Server
    IP Address                     VRF            Status
    --------------------------------------------------------
    10.38.22.33                                   Unknown

**STEP 5 VERDICT: PASS.**  Both commands are accepted.  Two things to note:

* the plain-text key `testing123` is **stored AES-encrypted** (`key 9 ...`) and is never
  displayed again, matching the `8`/`9` options STEP 2 enumerated;
* the server's `Status` starts at **`Unknown`**, not `Alive` -- the DUT has not yet spoken to
  it.  That is the same shape `show radius` has (§7E.4) and it makes `show tacacs+` a usable
