**`<id>/swi_d.cfg` was saved at this point** (2026-10-20 13:48 NZDT), after the case's setup
and before the measurement steps, from this `show running-config`.

## STEP 6 (designed) -- THE MEASUREMENT: a TACACS+-served login, proven on three instruments

Purpose: the subject of the case.  `tacuser`'s TACACS+ password is `testing123`; its LOCAL
password is `localonly1`.  A successful login with `testing123` can therefore ONLY have been
decided by the server.

    tools/tb capture tb277 cktac eth3 40 tac-accept.pcap tcp port 49     (in parallel with)
    tools/tb conlogin tb277 cktac u2 115200 --user tacuser --password testing123
        --expect user --restore-user tacuser --restore-password testing123

    LOGIN RESULT: USER  user=tacuser  seconds=0.6  prompt='awplus>'
    conlogin: expected USER, got USER -- MATCH
    conlogin: restore login as tacuser -> USER ('awplus>')

Two logins happened inside the window (the tested login and `conlogin`'s restore login), both
with the server password.

**Instrument 1 -- the DUT.**

    awplus# show tacacs+
    10.38.22.33                                   Alive          <- was `Unknown` in STEP 5

    awplus# show users
    Line    User            Host(s)  Idle      Location        Priv Idletime Timeout
    con 0   tacuser         idle     00:00:04  ttyS0           15   10       N/A

    awplus# show log tail 40      (device lines; IMISH command echoes removed)
    2026 Oct 20 00:50:03 authpriv.notice awplus login: PAM-tacplus: User tacuser is authenticated
    2026 Oct 20 00:50:05 authpriv.notice awplus login: PAM-tacplus: User tacuser is authenticated

